{"book":46,"chapter":5,"context":{"chapter":5,"title":"Sin the Church Ignored","summary":"Paul is shocked that the church tolerates a man living with his father's wife, and he tells them to remove him from their fellowship and to clear out the old 'leaven' of sin.","background":"A man was living with his stepmother, a union forbidden by the Law of Moses (Leviticus 18:8) and frowned on by Roman law too. The church was proud rather than grieved (v. 2). Paul mentions an earlier letter of his (v. 9) that has not survived.","customs":[{"term":"Leaven and Passover","verses":"5:6-8","note":"Before Passover, Jewish households searched out and removed all leaven (yeast) from their homes. Paul applies the practice: Christ the Passover lamb has been sacrificed, so the old leaven of sin must go."},{"term":"'Deliver… unto Satan'","verses":"5:5","note":"Putting the man outside the church's fellowship, back into the world's realm. Its exact meaning is debated, but the stated goal is that his spirit be saved."}],"watchFor":["Paul judges those inside the church, not outsiders (vv. 12–13).","The 'little leaven' proverb (v. 6) also appears in Galatians 5:9."],"connections":["Leviticus 18:8","Exodus 12:15-20","Deuteronomy 17:7","Galatians 5:9"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Ὅλως","Holōs","G3654","ADV","Actually"],["ἀκούεται","akouetai","G191","V-PPI-3S","is reported"],["ἐν","en","G1722","PREP","among"],["ὑμῖν","humin","G4771","P-2DP","you"],["πορνεία","porneia","G4202","N-NSF","sexual immorality"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["τοιαύτη","toiautē","G5108","D-NSF","such"],["πορνεία","porneia","G4202","N-NSF","sexual immorality"],["ἥτις","hētis","G3748","R-NSF","as"],["οὐδὲ","oude","G3761","CONJ-N","not even"],["ἐν","en","G1722","PREP","among"],["τοῖς","tois","G3588","T-DPN","the"],["ἔθνεσιν","ethnesin","G1484","N-DPN","pagans"],["ὀνομάζεται","onomazetai","G3687","V-PPI-3S","is named"],["ὥστε","hōste","G5620","CONJ","so as for"],["γυναῖκά","gunaika","G1135","N-ASF","[the] wife"],["τινα","t